# Approved portable executables, matched by SHA256. Empty by design.
#
# This is an allowlist, not a detection list: an entry here demotes rule 906142
# to logging level for that exact binary. Empty means nothing is approved yet,
# which is the correct default. It previously shipped with one fabricated entry,
# which made the list look populated while approving nothing.
#
# The key must be the whole hashes field as Sysmon reports it, including the
# algorithm prefix, because that is what the event carries:
#
#   SHA256=A1B2C3...:notepad-plus-plus
#
# To find the value for a binary you have decided to approve, read it from the
# alert that reported it rather than computing it separately, so that what you
# approve is what the agent actually saw.
